		{"id":"bbf8b5f8e0b73f8f","type":"text","text":"Top down/ \"Representative\" vs Distributed & Adaptive","x":495,"y":-275,"width":285,"height":60},
		{"id":"857b4b79d3148eaa","type":"text","text":"## Why digital (information) technology? What benefits does it offer?","x":-195,"y":-880,"width":400,"height":160,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"6336e00494e43d2a","type":"text","text":"Paint picture of how it can help us improve society in a tangible way","x":945,"y":-665,"width":250,"height":85},
		{"id":"dc3dbdd37f7cd244","type":"text","text":"Throughout history, civilizations have collapsed when they couldn't deal with the information complexity they created (Source?)","x":325,"y":-750,"width":250,"height":170},
		{"id":"899eec22514244ca","type":"text","text":"Digital tech can help us address our civilization's information complexity if we wield it well enough","x":590,"y":-720,"width":250,"height":140},
		{"id":"8fb99bbc1775d637","type":"text","text":"# Hypotheses of transformation","x":310,"y":-1120,"width":530,"height":80,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"6c4153de3300d863","type":"text","text":"# Experiments for a new world","x":310,"y":-1040,"width":530,"height":80,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"c956f40e42858e64","type":"text","text":"We are facing the Metacrisis, a crisis of cooperation and collaboration","x":260,"y":-910,"width":250,"height":110},
		{"id":"334fc038c5b7a152","type":"text","text":" Digital systems are highly adaptable, easy to experiment and evolve","x":590,"y":-940,"width":250,"height":90},
		{"id":"051340a17bcedd2b","type":"text","text":"Opportunities for collaboration at scale","x":575,"y":-830,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"98d42619663013a8","type":"text","text":"A living essay on the next evolution of information technologies, and how they might help us transform our world.","x":880,"y":-1080,"width":380,"height":120},
		{"id":"4c2993525c31b923","type":"text","text":"We are already seeing huge externalities from digital tech, it can either work for us or against us (big capacity for both regeneration and destruction at scale)","x":945,"y":-880,"width":275,"height":160},
		{"id":"f3a59d5001af9b4a","type":"text","text":"# Transition Steps","x":4245,"y":483,"width":375,"height":90,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"f6f68231fbe9cf10","type":"text","text":"Information Technology: \"the study or use of systems (especially computers and telecommunications) for storing, retrieving, and sending information.\" [Source](https://www.google.com/search?q=information+technology&rlz=1CDGOYI_enUS887US887&oq=information+tech&aqs=chrome.0.0i512j69i57j0i512l6j46i512j0i512.5876j0j7&hl=es&sourceid=chrome-mobile&ie=UTF-8)\nInformation tech is not just about computers, its all the ways we engage with information: culture, governance, economics etc. Digital systems are just the newest tools to facilitate this, also: writing, language, money, music, storytelling, laws are info tech.","x":1260,"y":-885,"width":378,"height":305},
		{"id":"e2692e9a15a2e3ef","type":"text","text":"Software is an extension of our brains (we are already cyborgs). Also, writing, language, math. \nThe kind of software we design shapes how we think & by extension how we behave at an individual & societal scale [[Inside the digital sensorium]]","x":1702,"y":-795,"width":338,"height":235},
		{"id":"9e1514e6710763a8","type":"text","text":"Building technology is philosophy in practice: \"Doing Philosophy\" [Source](https://twitter.com/tofth__)","x":1710,"y":-960,"width":250,"height":130},
